{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLTDVBeQvposAxh9yfXi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added the missing-tests Go helper with its fixtures and tests, and `make test` passes. `make lint` still fails, but on an existing fixture this change doesn't touch.\n\n- **Lint failure:** both `go vet ./...` and `gofmt -l .` report a syntax error in `internal/roles/testdata/docs/skips/src/_x.go`. `go vet ./internal/roles` passes, and the new files are gofmt-clean.\n- **Tests:** the new `TestMissingTests*` tests pass in about 8 seconds on a warm cache. `TestInitOpensPR` and `TestFSContents` pass unchanged, so the starter tree is unchanged.\n- **Starter tree:** in `internal/roles/roles.go` the embed line now lists `scanners/cve`, `scanners/docs` and `scanners/error-codes` instead of all of `scanners`. The plan's version left out `scanners/docs`, which has been added since, so I kept it in. Part 2 has to add `scanners/missing-tests` back.\n- **Fixtures:** I generated each `want.jsonl` from the helper once and checked it by hand against the severity table. The `build_tags` fixture expects empty output, so it only shows that tagged files add no findings.\n- **Design gap:** the design doesn't say what to do when a group name is over 256 bytes, which the scanner schema rejects. I replace it with `go:sha256:<hex>`.\n\nI wrote the report to `.ard/212/worker-engineer.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1213,"cache_read_input_tokens":70370,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1213},"output_tokens":501,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"909e7110-49e7-45da-a755-d313c94b7564","uuid":"beef3115-a622-46e1-84bb-009ffbdbc9d4","times